<rdf:Description rdf:about="">
<dc:identifier></dc:identifier>
<dc:title>Mapping the lymphatic system across body scales and expertise domains: A report from the 2021 National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute workshop at the Boston Lymphatic Symposium</dc:title>
<prism:doi></prism:doi>
<prism:url></prism:url>
<dc:creator><rdf:Bag><rdf:li>Dhruv Singhal</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Katy Börner</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Elliot L. Chaikof</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Michael Detmar</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Maija Hollmén</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Jeffrey J. Iliff</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Maxim Itkin</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Taija Makinen</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Guillermo Oliver</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Timothy P. Padera</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Ellen M. Quardokus</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Andrea J. Radtke</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Hiroo Suami</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Griffin M. Weber</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Ilsa I. Rovira</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Selen C. Muratoglu</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Zorina S. Galis</rdf:li>
</rdf:Bag></dc:creator>
<dc:description>Enhancing our understanding of lymphatic anatomy from the microscopic to the anatomical scale is essential to discern how the structure and function of the lymphatic system interacts with different tissues and organs within the body and contributes to health and disease.</dc:description>
<dc:subject><rdf:Bag><rdf:li>lymphatic disease</rdf:li><rdf:li>lymphedema</rdf:li><rdf:li>lymphatic research</rdf:li><rdf:li>mapping</rdf:li><rdf:li>lymphatic anatomy</rdf:li></rdf:Bag></dc:subject>
